course: dictionary
lesson: 1093
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Brahman is one of them. The words around it give you clues about which meaning is right. «Many Hindus believe the many gods are forms of one supreme reality, Brahman.» Here Brahman is a spirit: the one ultimate reality behind everything.
explain: Look for clue words. In «Brahman cattle», the word cattle tells you Brahman is an animal, a breed with a big hump on its shoulders. In «Brahmin priests», the word priests tells you it means a member of the highest priestly group. Brahmin is another spelling of the same meaning.
explain: «Hinduism is one of the oldest religions in the world; it began in India and has many traditions, and many Hindus see the many gods as forms of one supreme reality called Brahman.» The sentence gives the big idea: all the gods are forms of Brahman. Ask: which meaning fits here? Then put your meaning into the sentence and check it still makes sense.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: In Hinduism, Brahman is the one ultimate reality or supreme spirit behind everything.
fact: A Brahman is also a member of the highest priestly group in traditional Hindu society; Brahmin is another spelling.
fact: A Brahman is also a breed of cattle with a big hump on its shoulders, found in India, the USA and Australia.
fact: When a word has several meanings, the clue words in the sentence show you which one to use.
exercise: «Many Hindus believe the many gods are forms of one supreme reality, Brahman.» In this sentence, what is Brahman? | A breed of cattle with a big hump | *The one ultimate reality or supreme spirit behind everything | A type of temple | A member of the highest priestly group
exercise: «Brahman cattle» cope well with the heat. What is Brahman here? | A priest who leads the prayers | The one supreme spirit behind everything | *A breed of cattle with a big hump | A river in India
exercise: Which word in «Brahmin priests» tells you it means a group of people, not an animal? | *priests | spelling | cattle | Brahmin
test: «The Brahmin priests led the prayers at the temple.» What does Brahmin mean here? | A spelling mistake that should be removed | The one ultimate reality behind everything | A breed of cattle with a big hump | *A member of the highest priestly group in traditional Hindu society
test: «Brahman cattle grow a big hump on their shoulders.» Which meaning fits this sentence? | *A breed of cattle with a big hump | The one supreme spirit behind everything | A member of the highest priestly group | A kind of prayer
exam: In «many gods are forms of Brahman», why does Brahman mean the supreme spirit and not cattle? | Because Brahman always means a priest | Because the sentence has no clue words at all | *The words gods and forms of one supreme reality are the clues | Because cattle are always sacred in every religion
